% Hospital Beds and Accessories: LCD L33820 and its Policy Article A52508
% (DME MACs), read with NCD 280.7 (Hospital Beds). A policy program of the
% DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category,
% continued need, refills) and states when a claim for a hospital bed — fixed
% height (E0250, E0251, E0290, E0291, E0328), variable height (E0255, E0256,
% E0292, E0293), semi-electric (E0260, E0261, E0294, E0295, E0329), heavy
% duty extra wide (E0301, E0303), extra heavy duty (E0302, E0304) — or an
% accessory — trapeze equipment (E0910, E0940), heavy duty trapeze equipment
% (E0911, E0912), a bed cradle (E0280), side rails (E0305, E0310), a safety
% enclosure (E0316), a replacement mattress (E0271, E0272) — is REASONABLE
% AND NECESSARY. A total electric bed (E0265, E0266, E0296, E0297) is never
% covered ("the height adjustment feature is a convenience feature"), nor a
% bed the codes do not describe (E1399): no rule concludes them. A bed board
% (E0273, E0315) and an over bed table (E0274) are within the policy's scope
% but outside the benefit ("not primarily medical in nature"): no rule places
% them in a benefit category.
%
% How the criteria are read. The four criteria of a fixed height bed are
% alternatives ("one or more of the following criteria (1-4)"). Criteria 1
% and 2 — a medical condition requiring positioning of the body in ways not
% feasible with an ordinary bed, or such positioning to alleviate pain — are
% one clinical judgment, the judged template of dmepos.le "the finding F
% about B is established" (or unsupported), with who found it and why.
% Criteria 3 and 4 are what the record states: the head of the bed must be
% elevated N degrees most of the time (the threshold, 30, is in the rule) for
% one of the three named conditions (the shared template "the medical record
% of B documents C"), or traction equipment that can only be attached to a
% hospital bed is required. Each further bed type adds one finding; the
% weight classes read the beneficiary's weight in pounds. Where the LCD
% offers alternatives within one criterion (frequent changes and/or an
% immediate need; sit up, change position, or get in or out of bed) they are
% ONE finding with the alternatives as its reasons. The findings this policy
% reads, and the criterion each stands for:
%   positioning infeasible in ordinary bed (fixed height criteria 1 and 2:
%   a condition requiring positioning not feasible with an ordinary bed, or
%   positioning to alleviate pain); needs variable height for transfers
%   (variable height bed: a bed height different than a fixed height bed to
%   permit transfers to chair, wheelchair or standing position); needs
%   frequent changes in body position (semi-electric bed: frequent changes
%   in body position and/or an immediate need for a change in body
%   position); needs trapeze (trapeze equipment: to sit up because of a
%   respiratory condition, to change body position for other medical
%   reasons, or to get in or out of bed); bed cradle necessary (a bed
%   cradle: necessary to prevent contact with the bed coverings); side rails
%   required and safety enclosure required (required by the beneficiary's
%   condition); replacement mattress required (the beneficiary's condition
%   requires a replacement mattress).
% What the record states as fact — the head elevation and its condition,
% the traction equipment, the weight, that the bed is beneficiary owned,
% that a trapeze bar is used on an ordinary bed — is a scenario fact.
%
% NCD 280.7 is the general rule the LCD applies: its reasons for a hospital
% bed (positioning "in ways not feasible in an ordinary bed"; "special
% attachments that cannot be fixed and used on an ordinary bed") are the
% LCD's criteria 1-2 and 4; its variable height conditions (C) the LCD's
% transfer criterion; its electric adjustments (D) the semi-electric
% criterion. The NCD's added condition that "the patient can operate the
% controls" (D) is not in the LCD and is not modelled; nor is its
% prescription rule (B), which the standard written order of dmepos.le
% replaces.
%
% The LCD has no continued-coverage criteria of its own: a rental month after
% the first needs the continued need and use of dmepos.le. The Policy
% Article's policy-specific requirements are the face-to-face encounter and
% written order prior to delivery of Final Rule 1713 (E0290, E0301 and E0304
% are on the CMS list dmepos.le reads) and the KX/GA/GZ modifiers (billing,
% not modelled): the policy declares no documentation requirements of its own.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* requires the head of the bed elevated *a number* degrees most of the time; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* requires traction equipment that can only be attached to a hospital bed; undefined.
    *a device* is owned by the beneficiary; undefined.
    *an item* is used on an ordinary bed; undefined.
    % the knowledge base
    *a condition* is a qualifying condition for head elevation.
    bed accessory code *a code* is noncovered as not primarily medical in nature.
    % derived
    *an item* is a hospital bed.
    *an item* is a trapeze bar used on an ordinary bed.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed.
    the record of *a beneficiary* states a criterion for a fixed height hospital bed.
    *an item* meets the hospital bed coverage criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for trapeze equipment.

the knowledge base hospital beds includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base hospital beds includes:

LCD L33820 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33820".
the text of LCD L33820 is at "sources/lcd/L33820.txt".
Policy Article A52508 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52508".
the text of Policy Article A52508 is at "sources/article/A52508.txt".
NCD 280 7 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/ncd.aspx?ncdid=227".
the text of NCD 280 7 is at "sources/ncd/NCD_280.7.txt".

% What a hospital bed is: the codes of the LCD's five covered types and of
% the total electric bed (the Policy Article's coding guidelines describe
% each type; the list is the LCD's).
rule beds_hospital_bed with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "For any of the above hospital beds (plus those coded E1399 - see Policy Article Coding Guidelines), if documentation does not justify the medical need of the type of bed billed, payment will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
an item is a hospital bed
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0250", "E0251", "E0290", "E0291", "E0328", "E0255", "E0256", "E0292", "E0293", "E0260", "E0261", "E0294", "E0295", "E0329", "E0301", "E0303", "E0302", "E0304", "E0265", "E0266", "E0296", "E0297"].

% A trapeze bar attached to a bed, used on an ordinary bed (the Policy
% Article's exclusion; E0940 and E0912 are free standing).
rule beds_trapeze_ordinary_bed with provenance Policy Article A52508,
        confer "Trapeze bars attached to a bed (E0910, E0911) are noncovered when used on an ordinary bed":
an item is a trapeze bar used on an ordinary bed
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0910", "E0911"]
    and the item is used on an ordinary bed.

% The conditions of the head elevation criterion.
congestive heart failure is a qualifying condition for head elevation,
    as stated in LCD L33820, confer "due to congestive heart failure, chronic pulmonary disease, or problems with aspiration".
chronic pulmonary disease is a qualifying condition for head elevation,
    as stated in LCD L33820, confer "due to congestive heart failure, chronic pulmonary disease, or problems with aspiration".
problems with aspiration is a qualifying condition for head elevation,
    as stated in LCD L33820, confer "due to congestive heart failure, chronic pulmonary disease, or problems with aspiration".

% The accessories the Policy Article places outside the benefit.
bed accessory code "E0273" is noncovered as not primarily medical in nature,
    as stated in Policy Article A52508, confer "A bed board (E0273, E0315) is noncovered since it is not primarily medical in nature".
bed accessory code "E0315" is noncovered as not primarily medical in nature,
    as stated in Policy Article A52508, confer "A bed board (E0273, E0315) is noncovered since it is not primarily medical in nature".
bed accessory code "E0274" is noncovered as not primarily medical in nature,
    as stated in Policy Article A52508, confer "An over bed table (E0274, E0315) is noncovered because it is not primarily medical in nature".

section applicability is:

% The Policy Article's policy-specific requirements are the face-to-face
% encounter and WOPD of Final Rule 1713 (dmepos.le, by the CMS list) and the
% claim modifiers (billing): none of the policy's own.
hospital beds has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the beds, the accessories, and the bed
% boards and over bed tables the Policy Article excludes from the benefit.
rule beds_codes with provenance Policy Article A52508,
        confer "Hospital Beds are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is hospital beds
    if the code is in ["E0250", "E0251", "E0290", "E0291", "E0328", "E0255", "E0256", "E0292", "E0293", "E0260", "E0261", "E0294", "E0295", "E0329", "E0301", "E0303", "E0302", "E0304", "E0265", "E0266", "E0296", "E0297", "E0910", "E0940", "E0911", "E0912", "E0280", "E0305", "E0310", "E0316", "E0271", "E0272", "E0273", "E0274", "E0315"].

% Their benefit: durable medical equipment, except the bed board and the
% over bed table.
rule beds_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52508,
        confer "Hospital Beds are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is hospital beds
    and it is not the case that
        bed accessory code the code is noncovered as not primarily medical in nature.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Hospital beds: a bed is reasonable and necessary when the beneficiary meets
% the criteria of the type of bed billed. A total electric bed (E0265, E0266,
% E0296, E0297) has no rule: "A total electric hospital bed (E0265, E0266,
% E0296, and E0297) is not covered; the height adjustment feature is a
% convenience feature. Total electric beds will be denied as not reasonable
% and necessary." Nor has E1399.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule beds_covered with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "If the beneficiary does not meet any of the coverage criteria for any type of hospital bed it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a hospital bed
    and the item meets the hospital bed coverage criteria.

% A fixed height bed: one or more of criteria 1-4.
rule beds_fixed_height with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "A fixed height hospital bed (E0250, E0251, E0290, E0291, and E0328) is covered if one or more of the following criteria (1-4) are met":
an item meets the hospital bed coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0250", "E0251", "E0290", "E0291", "E0328"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed.

% The criteria are alternatives: what the record states (criteria 3 and 4)
% decides first; only when the record states neither is the positioning
% judgment (criteria 1 and 2) consulted — the "otherwise" is this model's
% device, so that a criterion the record establishes does not leave a
% judgment open beside it (the truth values are those of "one or more").
rule beds_fixed_height_criteria with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "is covered if one or more of the following criteria (1-4) are met":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed
    if the record of the beneficiary states a criterion for a fixed height hospital bed
    otherwise the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about the beneficiary is established.

% Criteria 1 and 2 are the positioning finding (its reasons: a medical
% condition requiring positioning not feasible with an ordinary bed, or
% positioning to alleviate pain; "Elevation of the head/upper body less than
% 30 degrees does not usually require the use of a hospital bed"), the
% "otherwise" line above; the passage of criterion 1:
% "The beneficiary has a medical condition which requires positioning of the
% body in ways not feasible with an ordinary bed", of criterion 2: "The
% beneficiary requires positioning of the body in ways not feasible with an
% ordinary bed in order to alleviate pain".

% Criterion 3: the head of the bed elevated more than 30 degrees most of the
% time, for one of the named conditions.
rule beds_criterion_3 with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "The beneficiary requires the head of the bed to be elevated more than 30 degrees most of the time due to congestive heart failure, chronic pulmonary disease, or problems with aspiration":
the record of a beneficiary states a criterion for a fixed height hospital bed
    if the beneficiary requires the head of the bed elevated a number degrees most of the time
    and the number > 30
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a qualifying condition for head elevation.

% Criterion 4: traction equipment.
rule beds_criterion_4 with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "The beneficiary requires traction equipment, which can only be attached to a hospital bed":
the record of a beneficiary states a criterion for a fixed height hospital bed
    if the beneficiary requires traction equipment that can only be attached to a hospital bed.

% A variable height bed: a fixed height criterion, and a bed height for
% transfers.
rule beds_variable_height with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "A variable height hospital bed (E0255, E0256, E0292, and E0293) is covered if the beneficiary meets one of the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed and requires a bed height different than a fixed height hospital bed to permit transfers to chair, wheelchair or standing position":
an item meets the hospital bed coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0255", "E0256", "E0292", "E0293"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed
    and the finding needs variable height for transfers about the beneficiary is established.

% A semi-electric bed: a fixed height criterion, and frequent changes in
% body position and/or an immediate need for a change.
rule beds_semi_electric with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "A semi-electric hospital bed (E0260, E0261, E0294, E0295, and E0329) is covered if the beneficiary meets one of the criteria for a fixed height bed and requires frequent changes in body position":
an item meets the hospital bed coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0260", "E0261", "E0294", "E0295", "E0329"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed
    and the finding needs frequent changes in body position about the beneficiary is established.

% A heavy duty extra wide bed: a fixed height criterion, and a weight over
% 350 pounds up to 600.
rule beds_heavy_duty with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "A heavy duty extra wide hospital bed (E0301, E0303) is covered if the beneficiary meets one of the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed and the beneficiary's weight is more than 350 pounds, but does not exceed 600 pounds":
an item meets the hospital bed coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0301", "E0303"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a number pounds
    and the number > 350
    and the number <= 600.

% An extra heavy duty bed: a fixed height criterion ("one of the criteria
% for a hospital bed"), and a weight over 600 pounds.
rule beds_extra_heavy_duty with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "An extra heavy-duty hospital bed (E0302, E0304) is covered if the beneficiary meets one of the criteria for a hospital bed and the beneficiary's weight exceeds 600 pounds":
an item meets the hospital bed coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0302", "E0304"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a fixed height hospital bed
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a number pounds
    and the number > 600.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Accessories.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Trapeze equipment: the finding, and (a bar attached to a bed) not used on
% an ordinary bed.
rule beds_trapeze with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "Trapeze equipment (E0910, E0940) is covered if the beneficiary needs this device to sit up because of a respiratory condition, to change body position for other medical reasons, or to get in or out of bed":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0910", "E0940"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for trapeze equipment
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a trapeze bar used on an ordinary bed.

rule beds_trapeze_criteria with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "the beneficiary needs this device to sit up because of a respiratory condition, to change body position for other medical reasons, or to get in or out of bed":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for trapeze equipment
    if the finding needs trapeze about the beneficiary is established.

% Heavy duty trapeze equipment: the regular criteria and a weight over 250
% pounds.
rule beds_heavy_duty_trapeze with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "Heavy duty trapeze equipment (E0911, E0912) is covered if the beneficiary meets the criteria for regular trapeze equipment and the beneficiary's weight is more than 250 pounds":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0911", "E0912"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for trapeze equipment
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a number pounds
    and the number > 250
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a trapeze bar used on an ordinary bed.

% A bed cradle.
rule beds_cradle with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "A bed cradle (E0280) is covered when it is necessary to prevent contact with the bed coverings":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0280"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding bed cradle necessary about the beneficiary is established.

% Side rails and safety enclosures: required by the condition, and an
% accessory of a bed that meets the coverage criteria (rails provided with
% the bed are billed in the bed's code, the Policy Article's Column II).
rule beds_side_rails with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "Side rails (E0305, E0310) or safety enclosures (E0316) are covered when they are required by the beneficiary's condition and they are an integral part of, or an accessory to, a covered hospital bed":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0305", "E0310"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding side rails required about the beneficiary is established
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device meets the hospital bed coverage criteria.

rule beds_safety_enclosure with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "Side rails (E0305, E0310) or safety enclosures (E0316) are covered when they are required by the beneficiary's condition and they are an integral part of, or an accessory to, a covered hospital bed":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0316"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding safety enclosure required about the beneficiary is established
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device meets the hospital bed coverage criteria.

% A replacement mattress, for a beneficiary owned hospital bed.
rule beds_mattress with provenance LCD L33820,
        confer "If a beneficiary's condition requires a replacement innerspring mattress (E0271) or foam rubber mattress (E0272) it will be covered for a beneficiary owned hospital bed":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0271", "E0272"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding replacement mattress required about the beneficiary is established
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a hospital bed
    and the device is owned by the beneficiary.
